From c77d7a551d2b83041e231cf24ed05ca1da78873b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dwc2d: wait with a yield loop, never with nanosleep

A nanosleep in dwc2d sometimes never returns. dwc2d's main loop then
waits for good without using the CPU, and since the main loop also serves
the network scheme, netstack waits with it: "main loop stuck in read from
the network device", the network gone until a power cycle (#151). In Pi
test 326 a 382 MB download into the SD card stalled 3 of 3 times on main;
in test 342 dwc2d's main thread sat in state US with its CPU time frozen,
and main with the sleeps replaced (experiment usb-hub-drop) completed 3
of 3. The LAN7800 link check every second polls the MII with 1 ms sleeps,
so a running network called nanosleep a few times a second.

Every sleep in dwc2d now goes through delay(), which yields the CPU until
the time has passed. The longest waits are during enumeration (up to
500 ms); in normal running only the 1 ms polls remain. The lost wakeup
itself is a kernel matter and not fixed here.

Taken from experiment usb-hub-drop (base 0083), which keeps its other
changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
